WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.963
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module.

2
00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:05.907
You'll name the client's
platforms and prerequisites,

3
00:00:05.907 --> 00:00:08.249
and the configurations it doesn't support.

4
00:00:08.249 --> 00:00:12.054
You'll package it as a Win32 app
with Learn's install command,

5
00:00:12.054 --> 00:00:14.150
return codes and detection rule.

6
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.507
You'll explain why D N S over H T
T P S is turned off in browsers,

7
00:00:18.507 --> 00:00:22.500
and why the hardening
remediation waits for ring two.

8
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.402
You'll enable the Microsoft
traffic profile for a pilot group,

9
00:00:26.402 --> 00:00:28.162
with source I P restoration.

10
00:00:28.162 --> 00:00:32.538
And you'll compute client coverage, and
the share of sign-ins the service carries.

11
00:00:32.538 --> 00:00:35.378
You need Module 1, with the telemetry on,

12
00:00:35.378 --> 00:00:40.613
and a skim of Devices and Endpoints,
chapter four, for the Win32 app model.

13
00:00:40.613 --> 00:00:43.820
The lab runs in a test
tenant, never production.
